# Media Workbench v2 — screen comp R2: Prepare (drafted-prompt diff) + Suitability card (conventional document, macOS light appearance)
schema: "0.4"
id: mw-screen-prepare-suitability
type: image
service: gemini
model: gemini-3.1-flash-image
quality: high
prompt:
  text: |
    A straight-on screenshot of a macOS 14 Sonoma app window, light system appearance, SF Pro type, traffic lights, unified toolbar titled "pricing-hero" with a small subtitle "Request R-014". The app is a media-generation workbench; this screen reviews an AI-drafted prompt before any money is spent generating.

    Left: the translucent source-list sidebar: "Requests 3" (selected), "Library", "Runs 2", "Styles", divider, "Settings".

    Centre (about 55% width): a readable document pane showing a short YAML file in SF Mono as a diff with exactly seven numbered lines, gutter numbers 1 to 7 in order. Lines 1, 2, 3, 4 and 7 are additions: pale green background with a "+" in the gutter, reading exactly "+type: image", "+service: gemini", "+width: 2560", "+height: 1600", "+palette: house". Line 5 is pale red with a "−" in the gutter: "−quality: draft". Line 6 is pale green with a "+": "+quality: high". Nothing else in the pane — no ellipsis line, no line of dots, no trailing rows. A thin bar above the diff with three buttons: "Accept", "Accept partial", "Reject".

    Right (about 30% width): one white rounded card titled "Suitability", with a small chip "alibaba · decision-model-preview".
    - Large bold text "Needs revision" with "52%" at right.
    - Directly under it, one horizontal element divided into four adjoining coloured segments of unequal widths, the widest one orange, each segment carrying exactly its own text: "ready 31", "needs-revision 52", "wrong-type 11", "mismatch 6". All four segments fit inside the card with a small margin — nothing clipped at the card edge.
    - Two rows, each: exactly ten small square cells in one row — count them, exactly 10 cells, nine dark grey and one white, the white one at position 9 of 10 — plus a thin vertical tick directly above the white cell. The row labels are "Specificity 6.4" and "Constraint fit 7.8" with no other words anywhere on these two rows.
    - One short reason line: "Usage says dark bg; prompt omits it".
    - A row of small rounded provenance chips: "house:palette", "project:voice", "house:construction".
    - Buttons stacked at the bottom of the card: one blue primary "Revise with feedback", a secondary "Change type…", and a plain text link "Generate anyway".

    Document-like, readable, calm; semantic colour only on the emphatic text described above. On screen, only the exact strings quoted above appear — no other words.
  negative: >
    garbled text, lorem ipsum, watermark, mobile frame, browser chrome, Windows UI,
    perspective tilt, synthesizer/audio-hardware look, CAD tool, manuscript editor,
    chat bubbles, dark mode, pie chart, gauge dial, emoji icons, long paragraphs of code,
    ellipsis lines of dots, stray caption text, cells beyond ten per row, clipped text
  style: "UI design screen comp, straight-on screenshot framing, no perspective, no camera tilt, crisp pixel-sharp interface"
output:
  formats:
    - format: png
      quality: 95
  dimensions:
    width: 2560
    height: 1600
    aspect_ratio: "16:10"
eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.7
  criteria:
    depicts_the_product:
      weight: 0.4
      description: "reads as a media-generation request/review/grading tool, specifically a pre-flight review of an AI-drafted prompt file with a judge verdict on whether it is suitable to generate"
    follows_spec:
      weight: 0.35
      description: "shows (1) a YAML prompt as a diff with Accept / Accept partial / Reject; (2) a Suitability card with a four-segment probability bar (ready / needs-revision / wrong-type / mismatch), not only the winner; (3) 10-cell distribution strips for specificity and constraint fit; (4) provenance chips and a 'Generate anyway' override path"
    macos_native:
      weight: 0.25
      description: "reads as a native macOS 14 light-appearance document window with source-list sidebar, SF type and system buttons"
  reject_if:
    - depicts a different product category (chat app, code IDE only, CAD tool, manuscript editor, audio hardware, web page)
    - primary labels (Suitability, Needs revision, the four outcome labels) are unreadable or garbled
tags: [screen-comp, macos, media-workbench, v2]
